{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117939","id":3461103188,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7OTD5U","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117939","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117939.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117939.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117939","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117939/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117939/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117939/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/53be22e910d03666429480d6e1d44a12b79086e8","number":117939,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Handle Tree's root and foreign item drops better","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR fixes three minor problems that appeared after #112993, including one regression.\r\n\r\n- First, it closes #117895.\r\n- Second, the new reliance of Tree on `selected_item` for the improved rejection of recursive child drops as well as for the unchanged position drop indicator necessitated a way to distinguish a drop originating from a foreign Tree vs an internal one, since foreign drops could be negated by an unrelated selection in the receiving Tree. `dragging_within_self` accomplishes this, and is the most minimal way of doing so without a TreeItem-based refactor of drop data.\r\n- Third, dragging a node from SceneTreeDock \"onto\" a folder in FileSystemDock is supposed to request that folder as the drop location in the \"Save As...\" prompt. However, due to FileSystemDock implicitly \"selecting\" the hovered TreeItem when receiving this kind of drop, our prior negation of dropping onto self was preventing this, setting \"res://\" as the location, while sibling drops still worked fine. This has been fixed, and is a side-effect of the last change. In the future, it would most probably be best to change FileSystemDock's foreign drop behaviour into a superficial theme type for its drop indicator.\r\n\r\nFurther follow ups entail a deeper dive into individual Tree implementations, and while that may lead to these changes being whittled down in the future, they are not hacky and should generally benefit all Trees.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":""